From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upload the internal library documents from one manifest, and
 register the affiliate app guide.

docs/sql/0268_affiliate_app_guide_internal.tidb.sql registers "How to Create an
App for an Affiliate" as an internal document: visibility 'internal',
isPublished 0, category 'Internal', fileKey
library-documents/internal/how-to-create-an-app-for-an-affiliate.md.

A row on its own is not a document. The bytes have to sit in the private bucket
at that exact key, or the admin Open button answers 404. 0255 uploads the Marazzi
proposal with a script that hard-codes one PDF. This patch turns that script into
a loop over one manifest, so both documents go up from the same command and a
third one is a one-line change.

  shared/internalLibraryDocuments.ts
      The manifest. Title, description, category, file name, storage key, url,
      mimeType, sizeBytes, SHA-256 and sortOrder, for every hand-registered
      internal document. cabinet-frontend ships the same file, so its SQL is
      generated from it and cannot drift from what this importer uploads.

  server/scripts/import-internal-library-documents.ts
      Loops over the manifest. Before each upload it checks the committed bytes
      against sizeBytes and SHA-256 and stops on a mismatch, so a truncated or
      re-encoded file fails loudly instead of becoming a broken download. It
      still uploads bytes only: no INSERT, no UPDATE, no visibility change. A
      missing row is a message, not a failure, so the upload can run first.

  server/internalLibraryDocuments.test.ts
      Extended. Every manifest document must point at a committed file with a
      key in the private prefix, and the guide's SQL must be plain, one statement
      per line, internal and unpublished.

  docs/sql/0268_affiliate_app_guide_internal.tidb.sql
      Copied verbatim from cabinet-frontend, which is the single source for the
      TiDB paste.

Apply from the cabinet-backend repository root:

    git apply /path/to/cabinet-backend-affiliate-app-guide-internal.patch

Then, in this order, on the machine whose DATABASE_URL and
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY point at production:

  1. pnpm exec tsx server/scripts/import-internal-library-documents.ts
     with FRONTEND_REPO_ROOT pointing at the cabinet-frontend checkout. This puts
     the guide (and the Marazzi PDF, re-uploaded identically) in the private
     bucket. Upload first: the script needs no row, and doing it in this order
     means the admin Open button works the moment the row exists.

  2. Paste docs/sql/0268_affiliate_app_guide_internal.tidb.sql in the TiDB
     editor, line by line. Stop if statement 1 returns a row.

  3. Re-run the importer once. Nothing changes except the log line, which should
     now read "Row N is internal: admin only".

Frontend: cabinet-frontend pull request on cursor/affiliate-app-guide-internal-7794.

